<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 17:26:56 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>'Life in Gaza simply miserable': Amid flooding, lack of aid, conditions 'worsen' for Palestinians</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/life-in-gaza-simply-miserable-amid-flooding-lack-of-aid-conditions-worsen-for-palestinians</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Shaina Low, Communication Adviser for the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC). Thirteen months into what she describes as a "so-called ceasefire," the humanitarian crisis in Gaza continues to deepen, exposing the profound gap between diplomatic commitments and the lived realities of Palestinian civilians. In an interview with France 24, Shayna Low, communications adviser in Palestine for the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC), describes a population confronting winter flooding, repeated displacement, deteriorating shelter conditions and persistent restrictions on humanitarian assistance. "Life in Gaza is simply miserable." Low urges Israel to "open all the crossings, lift the restrictions, let aid in."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3d3edca-dc60-11f1-8648-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-160607-161526-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3d3edca-dc60-11f1-8648-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-160607-161526-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e94ce432-dc60-11f1-96d5-cb6fc6fe985c</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 17:26:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Iran 'has mistaken perception' of US midterm result, expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-sees-golden-opportunity-for-a-sweetheart-deal-after-us-midterms-expert-says</link><description>
A leading commentator on Iran says the country sees the results of the US midterm elections as giving them a golden opportunity for a sweet deal. Paymon Azmoudeh from Forward Global was speaking amid conflicting statements from the key players about whether there will be further US military action in Iran. President Donald Trump says that renewed strikes on Iran are "highly unlikely" if talks progress. However, Iran's foreign minister says the midterms have brought a ⁠pause to mediators' work. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf8bded8-dc41-11f1-bc20-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d352b274.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf8bded8-dc41-11f1-bc20-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d352b274.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">840f214c-dc20-11f1-8b82-83ba838a7e78</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 13:49:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi Arabia intercepts Houthi missiles as Riyadh's Aramco building damaged</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-saudi-arabia-intercepts-houthi-missiles-as-riyadh-s-aramco-building-damaged</link><description>
Saudi Arabia intercepted incoming missiles from Yemen's Houthi rebels targeting the kingdom's capital and other regions on Sunday, November 8, with falling debris damaging a building belonging to the state-owned oil giant Aramco in Riyadh’s financial district. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24a0a774-dc27-11f1-ad5f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6369a9a0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24a0a774-dc27-11f1-ad5f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6369a9a0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d95bd950-dc26-11f1-bf73-a7a7016cb462</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 10:41:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel's opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has six weeks to form a government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-israel-s-opposition-leader-gadi-eisenkot-has-six-weeks-to-form-a-government</link><description>
Israeli President Isaac Herzog formally gave opposition politician Gadi Eisenkot the first chance to form the next government Sunday evening, leaving Eisenkot six weeks to try to put together a coalition to oust Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cbef71e4-dc23-11f1-882d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f52ea606.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cbef71e4-dc23-11f1-882d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f52ea606.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">396313d0-dc23-11f1-9ef6-d590fdfa7516</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 10:36:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli opposition leader Eisenkot begins the hard work of forging a coalition government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-israeli-opposition-leader-eisenkot-begins-the-hard-work-of-forging-a-coalition-government</link><description>
Israel's ex-military chief Gadi Eisenkot was tapped by President Isaac Herzog to try to form a government Sunday evening. But his lack of a clear majority in parliament will make trying to forge a coalition alongside the country's divided minor parties an uphill struggle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be4c1c22-dbb5-11f1-bbd7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T152158Z-1569314181-RC2RJOASDUSW-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be4c1c22-dbb5-11f1-bbd7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T152158Z-1569314181-RC2RJOASDUSW-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">369dc2a8-dbb5-11f1-8464-4d6ebdc8c05c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 21:10:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be4c1c22-dbb5-11f1-bbd7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T152158Z-1569314181-RC2RJOASDUSW-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg">© Ronen Zvulun, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gadi Eisenkot receives mandate to form government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-receives-mandate-to-form-government</link><description>
Israel's opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has officially been tasked with forming the country's next government, following a formal announcement by President Isaac Herzog. He now has up to six weeks to negotiate with potential coalition partners and secure a parliamentary majority. While an alliance with Arab Israeli parties appears to be the easiest option mathematically, it remains politically sensitive. Eisenkot must now navigate difficult negotiations to build a coalition capable of replacing Benjamin Netanyahu. Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/608ffe0e-db93-11f1-85ef-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-160801-161121-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/608ffe0e-db93-11f1-85ef-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-160801-161121-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65b815e2-db93-11f1-9ee7-4943b8d2bb10</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:58:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen's humanitarian crisis worsens</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens</link><description>
One month into the Yemeni government's offensive against the Iran-aligned Houthis, fighting continues to escalate along the Red Sea coast. Meanwhile, the humanitarian crisis is worsening, with hundreds of thousands of people displaced and the country facing the threat of catastrophe. Rula Amin, Senior Communications Advisor and spokesperson at UNHCR at Amman, in Jordan, shares further details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61e95800-db7e-11f1-961e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140416-140658-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61e95800-db7e-11f1-961e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140416-140658-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6735dcac-db7e-11f1-b6b0-a3bc1c7deeec</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:22:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli president officially tasks Eisenkot with forming government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-middle-east-live-riyadh-financial-district-targeted-deadly-strikes-yemen-israel-eisenkot-netanyahu-coalition-government-elections</link><description>
Israeli President Isaac Herzog on Sunday officially tasked ex-military chief Gadi Eisenkot with trying to form a government after neither Eisenkot's bloc nor that or incumbent Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu won a clear majority in Israel's October 27 elections. Eisenkot now has up to six weeks to form a coalition government. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f71c892a-db87-11f1-9c18-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T151738Z-84214136-RC2RJOAONV9B-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f71c892a-db87-11f1-9c18-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T151738Z-84214136-RC2RJOAONV9B-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f9136bc-db58-11f1-b6e9-1d122f9c1034</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:47:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f71c892a-db87-11f1-9c18-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T151738Z-84214136-RC2RJOAONV9B-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg">© Ronen Zvulun, Reuters</source><dc:creator>Louise NORDSTROM</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel's Arab-led parties gain influence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-s-arab-led-parties-gain-influence</link><description>
Arab-led parties have endorsed Gadi Eisenkot despite his ruling out a coalition with them. Their support is driven by a shared goal: removing Benjamin Netanyahu from power. But could these parties ultimately hold the balance of power in forming Israel's next government? Antonia Kerrigan reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dec0c3da-db57-11f1-b79b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-100714-100924-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dec0c3da-db57-11f1-b79b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-100714-100924-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3c19d0a-db57-11f1-afce-7d507642ff15</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:43:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gaza: Heavy rain inundates thousands of tents</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gaza-heavy-rain-inundates-thousands-of-tents</link><description>
Heavy rainfall has flooded thousands of tents sheltering displaced Palestinians across the Gaza Strip, including in Deir al-Balah. Residents say overflowing sewage has mixed with the floodwater, further worsening already dire living conditions. Families are struggling to salvage their belongings, building makeshift earthen barriers and trying to drain the water by hand. Many have seen essential items soaked and rendered unusable, adding to the hardship faced by those already displaced.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25796fa2-db58-11f1-946f-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-100942-101123-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25796fa2-db58-11f1-946f-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-100942-101123-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2ac0b998-db58-11f1-a8f1-2946bdd1dc7c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:42:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's Houthis claim attack on Aramco skyscraper in Riyadh</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-yemen-s-houthis-claim-attack-on-aramco-building-in-riyadh-s-financial-district</link><description>
A skyscraper belonging to Saudi oil giant Aramco was hit by a Houthi-claimed attack on Sunday, blowing out windows across several floors but causing no casualties. The Iran-aligned group has repeatedly targeted Aramco facilities and infrastructure.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e783f10-db4c-11f1-abfd-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/7f554331a6cdd64418e7973b0fb73c45bab02694.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e783f10-db4c-11f1-abfd-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/7f554331a6cdd64418e7973b0fb73c45bab02694.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0f9aa748-db4c-11f1-9878-c523b432589c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 08:11:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e783f10-db4c-11f1-abfd-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/7f554331a6cdd64418e7973b0fb73c45bab02694.jpg">© Fayez Nureldine, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli president picks Netanyahu's rival Eisenkot to try to form government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government</link><description>
Israeli President Isaac Herzog picked former military chief Gadi Eisenkot to try to form a government, he said in a statement Saturday. Last month's parliamentary elections left neither Eisenkot nor Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu with a clear path to building a majority.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b98cb8f6-dae1-11f1-8c71-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-27T234936Z-337143780-RC2ZBOAVPW2L-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b98cb8f6-dae1-11f1-8c71-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-27T234936Z-337143780-RC2ZBOAVPW2L-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">75d30d4e-dae2-11f1-8579-699531bb8af2</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 19:37:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b98cb8f6-dae1-11f1-8c71-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-27T234936Z-337143780-RC2ZBOAVPW2L-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-ELECTION.jpg">© Shir Torem, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel coalition talks gain momentum</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-coalition-talks-gain-momentum</link><description>
Following inconclusive elections in Israel, opposition candidate Gadi Eisenkot says he is confident of securing the mandate to form a government, as President Isaac Herzog prepares to nominate the first candidate. Eisenkot claims he is making progress in efforts to oust long-serving Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c5335f2-daa4-11f1-8704-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-120418-120535-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c5335f2-daa4-11f1-8704-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-120418-120535-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">211bb6d6-daa4-11f1-bbe8-03bc64c04bde</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 12:12:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen: 30 dead in strikes on Taiz market</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-30-dead-in-strikes-on-taiz-market</link><description>
At least 30 people have reportedly been killed in an attack on a market in Yemen’s Taiz province, with Houthi rebels blaming Saudi airstrikes. Government forces and local authorities have disputed the claim, instead accusing the Houthis of indiscriminate fire. The province has witnessed intense clashes in recent weeks and is home to around half of the more than 300,000 people displaced by the latest fighting. Caroline Baum reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9da14e8a-da8d-11f1-9c90-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-090700-090851-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9da14e8a-da8d-11f1-9c90-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-090700-090851-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a297adee-da8d-11f1-b71c-09c09631d97d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 09:37:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Is Israel opposition figure Gadi Eisenkot going to replace Benjamin Netanyahu?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-is-israel-opposition-figure-gadi-eisenkot-going-to-replace-benjamin-netanyahu</link><description>
In Israel, Gadi Eisenkot emerged on Thursday, November 5, as the frontrunner to be tasked with forming a government. This comes after one of the two main parties representing ultra-Orthodox Jewish voters – a longtime ally of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's coalition – declined to recommend any candidate for the task. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebb71fde-d9cd-11f1-a086-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-04af7880.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebb71fde-d9cd-11f1-a086-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-04af7880.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8163f792-d9cd-11f1-b042-e7fb1d136a6b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:25:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel's Eisenkot claims 'progress' in coalition talks as opposition eases on ultra-Orthodox draft</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261106-israel-s-eisenkot-claims-significant-progress-in-coalition-talks-as-opposition-eases-on-ultra-orthodox-draft</link><description>
Israeli opposition candidate Gadi Eisenkot said on Friday he was making "significant progress" in forming a government to oust Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu as one of his possible coalition partners walked back demands that ultra-Orthodox Jews complete military service and signalled a willingness to hold talks with the community.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ff0f7b4-d9f0-11f1-85f8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26300857503629.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ff0f7b4-d9f0-11f1-85f8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26300857503629.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">58be440a-d9d7-11f1-81a3-d394862481ca</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 11:43:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ff0f7b4-d9f0-11f1-85f8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26300857503629.jpg">© Baz Ratner, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel president to announce Sunday who will form new government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-israel-president-to-announce-sunday-who-will-form-new-government</link><description>
Israeli President Isaac Herzog said he will announce on Sunday, November 8, whom he will task with trying to form a new government, following post-election talks with all party leaders. 46 parliament members recommended Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, while 67 backed his opponent Gadi Eisenkot. Seven lawmakers abstained.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ead5c768-d9c9-11f1-b93b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-19a34eeb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ead5c768-d9c9-11f1-b93b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-19a34eeb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b3618c9a-d9c9-11f1-a51a-8fbe1edd1a21</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:39:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Netanyahu rival Eisenkot secures broad backing in bid to form government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-netanyahu-rival-eisenkot-secures-broad-backing-in-bid-to-form-government</link><description>
Israeli President Isaac Herzog said he will announce on Sunday, November 8, whom he will task with trying to form a new government, after the opposition's Gadi Eisenkot secured a commanding number of recommendations to replace Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ca4b03da-d9c6-11f1-9cf2-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5edc64d1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ca4b03da-d9c6-11f1-9cf2-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5edc64d1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1bb0bd98-d9c5-11f1-95c7-55c37032bbe8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:02:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel's Arab list backs Eisenkot as Netanyahu loses ultra-Orthodox support</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-israel-main-arab-list-backs-eisenkot-to-form-government-after-election</link><description>
Israel's largest Arab party grouping said Thursday it would recommend opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot to form the next government, potentially bolstering his bid after Arab-majority lists won a record 19 seats in last week's election and Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu lost the support of an allied religious party.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29eef780-d925-11f1-85c3-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4MA4Z2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29eef780-d925-11f1-85c3-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4MA4Z2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b73f77c2-d925-11f1-8916-039cf3b813a7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:43:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29eef780-d925-11f1-85c3-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4MA4Z2.jpg">© Jack Guez, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthi missiles fired at Medina intercepted, Saudi coalition says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-houthi-missiles-fired-at-medina-intercepted-saudi-coalition-says</link><description>
